From 8787c96a288bf3443df9a34d839068e8d1aa44ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:58:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 686/705] hw/arm: yosemite5: populate the FRU EEPROMs

Back nine of the ten FRU EEPROMs with images read from hardware, so
guest firmware can identify the medusa board, paddle board, SCM, BSM,
E1.S backplane, CXL board, MB, CPU and OCP NIC instead of finding them
blank. The CLKGEN FRU was absent from the sampled chassis and stays
blank.

The content is sanitized: part and serial numbers masked, dates fixed,
asset tags replaced, distinct originals kept distinct. The OCP NIC
carries an OEM MultiRecord whose contents are undocumented; the record
is kept and its body zeroed. The CPU FRU declares a MultiRecord area
holding no valid record chain, so the image keeps its product area
alone.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_yosemite5.c | 360 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 351 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_yosemite5.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_yosemite5.c
index 2bfa6cf504..81a10a39a9 100644
